{
  "purpose": "Byte-level golden vectors for the type-preserving canonical encoding of fin.evidence.structured_snapshot v1 (specs/structured-corpus-evidence.md, Type-preserving digest). Python and TypeScript must reproduce canonical_json and digest byte-for-byte from the same snapshot. These vectors are a NEW profile: ADR 0092's legacy textified digest lives in data/conformance/evidence/database_row/digest_worksheet.json and is unchanged.",
  "digest_form": "lowercase hexadecimal SHA-256 of the UTF-8 canonical_json bytes; no algorithm prefix. The legacy profile prefixes 'sha256:' and the two spellings are deliberately distinct.",
  "encoding_rules": [
    "types stay distinct: null/true/false/string/array/object/number never collide",
    "numbers: reject non-finite, fractional, and outside +/- (2**53 - 1); accepted integers normalize to base-10 text, zero encodes as 0",
    "object keys sort by UTF-8 bytes at every level; array order is preserved; no whitespace",
    "strings: escape \" and \\ only; U+0000-U+001F as lowercase six-character \\u00xx; every other scalar emitted directly in UTF-8; no Unicode normalization",
    "null, true and false are literal",
    "an unpaired surrogate is refused, not repaired"
  ],
